"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole and launched in Q3 2023. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate and expanded its team with experts in machine learning and cloud computing. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms. The executive board approved a $2M budget, though an update later adjusted the project budget to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration, with an additional $55,000 allocated for compliance training and audits. Key upcoming events include a kickoff meeting on July 15th, a team meeting on August 1st to discuss budget allocations, and a findings discussion on August 5th. Stakeholders are asked to provide feedback on the prototype by the end of November, and new security protocols (MFA and encryption) will take effect in January."
